  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase V: Global Led Priorities to Carry Out Principled, Effective, and Accountable Responses for the Benefit of Crisis-Affected Populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The need for lifesaving humanitarian assistance and protection is at an all-time high in 2022. New waves of violence and protracted armed conflict, climatic shocks such as floods, droughts, or earthquakes, and emerging and recurrent epidemics and diseases have pushed millions of people to live in extremely dire conditions. IOM stepped up to provide support to a number of large emergencies, higher than at any other time in its history, stretching its capacity to the limit. As the institutional lead on directing operational activities, setting strategic policy, and fostering strategic partnerships in support of crisis affected populations, IOM&apos;s Department of Operations and Emergencies must continuously adapt and strengthen its ability to respond effectively and efficiently to the complex challenges facing the world. This institutional strengthening project contributes to ensuring that IOM is better equipped to respond to emergencies in a principled, effective, and accountable manner. To achieve this overarching objective, IOM is implementing its capacity building strategy for humanitarian response and is consolidating its work in four priority areas which are closely interrelated and lead to mutually reinforcing outcomes: good programming; institutional capacity; data and evidence; and information management and digitalization.</narrative>
  </description>
